{
  "case_id": "2001-01-455",
  "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument next in No. 01-455, Franconia Associates v. the United States, and the Grass Valley Terrace v. United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Eckland, you -- you began by saying you're seeking fair compensation for something."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeff H. Eckland",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ECKLAND: We are -- Justice Scalia, we are seeking compensation for the breach of contract."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners' counsel (Mr. Eckland)",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ECKLAND: In general, yes, that's true, Your Honor. But here the petitioners sued within 6 years of the actual breach."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Unnamed Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: And in fact, you did not sue until after the passage of 6 years."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Unnamed Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, the Government -- the Government cannot -- cannot break a contract then."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent's counsel (Mr. Roberts)",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROBERTS: Our position is that there is an actual breach at the time that the statute is passed, and it's a breach of -- of the promise that the Government made that it wouldn't impose additional legal restrictions on prepayment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: All right. If that is so, then exactly the same thing is true in a private contract when there has been an anticipatory breach."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Roberts",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My -- my argument is not that this is an anticipatory breach. The -- our -- our principal submission is that this is a present breach, but -- but it's a present breach of a promise that the Government --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: All right. But if it's just a background principle, I would worry about the practical consequence being of people, particularly in real estate contracts, having to study every regulation, every statute in order to tell their clients what to do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Roberts",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I don't think it discourages them, Your Honor, because they -- they can sue and their damages are measurable, and they can get the damages. The likelihood that interest rates are going to go up or that interest rates are going to go down and -- and other possibilities are -- are reflected in the -- in the change in the value of the loans and they're measurable at that time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeff H. Eckland",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government has not been able to cite to one case in which a congressional statute has been treated differently, in other words, that it constitutes an immediate breach of a contract."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeff H. Eckland",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the petitioners' briefs, we have a total of six cases that make the distinction between a congressional statute as being merely a repudiation and the breach not occurring until there has been some adverse agency action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeff H. Eckland",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Here it's clear that since the petitioners can reach their central right of opting out of this program upon prepayment -- and the statistics show that -- it can't be that the statute is an immediate breach. A breach occurs only if and when the agency acts and denies a prepayment request."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-01-455",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6fc2e64bc15950fc970e829eee6df3f41d447e93b457e61104e290bf853c9a3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6fc2e64bc15-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 12:02 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
